{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081442Z_dev-03_staged_1ede", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For ψψ̄ → h2h2, Kim, Lee, Park and Shin chose m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV as their best fit. They gave ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10⁻²⁶ cm³ s⁻¹, with Ωh² = 0.121. The best fit (χ² = 23.19, p-value 0.39) needed a J-factor scaling of 𝒥 = 2.2. The paper defines this as J̄ = 𝒥 × J̄_canonical, so the canonical J-factor was scaled up by a factor of 2.2. The paper states this definition in its bb̄ section, not in the h2h2 section.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.1"}]}, "turns": 5, "seconds": 14.565, "tool_calls": 6, "tool_result_chars": 28786, "input_tokens": 12, "output_tokens": 968, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 16684, "cache_read_input_tokens": 27954, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:14:57+00:00"}
